> Count dense work and admit complete histories before execution

After k completed sweeps on n unknowns, the dense implementation has assigned kn
coordinates, divided kn times and executed kn(n−1) off-diagonal products. Its
post-sweep residual checks add kn² dense products and k+1 norm evaluations,
including the initial norm of b without a matrix product. Zero coefficients are
still visited. These are algorithmic counts, not floating-operation counts or
elapsed time. This dense API uses O(kn²) arithmetic and O(n) extra ordinary storage
beyond the input matrix; a sparse implementation would need its own storage and
traversal contract.

Full histories copy two n-vectors per coordinate and one per completed sweep,
so their extra storage is O(kn²). Admission for a requested maximum K is

$$
H(n,K)=n+1+K\{n(1+2n)+(1+n)\}\quad(n>0),\qquad H(0,K)=1.
$$
\alttext(Count the initial n-vector and one residual, then for every requested sweep count n coordinate metadata records with two n-vectors each and one sweep metadata record with its n-vector; an empty system needs one residual entry.)

The units mix vector values and fixed-schema metadata records as documented by
the API; they are not bytes or peak RAM. Root/work metadata, final ordinary output,
original A and b, working state and allocator storage are excluded. The default
entry cap is one million; zero disables only the optional quota. Complete count,
capacity and quota checks precede initialization or history allocation. Even a
zero RHS receives no early-success discount from the requested nonempty-system
bound. The actual retained count can be smaller when convergence occurs early.
There is no truncation, numerical replay or partial returned history, and inputs
and snapshots have independent ownership. The older residual-only trace keeps
its separate online cap on actual residual entries, including the initial one.

```{cpp, results="markdown", file="figures/seidel_work.svg", flags="-std=c++23 -O2 $(pkg-config --cflags --libs datamunge) -Wl,-rpath,$(pkg-config --variable=libdir datamunge)"}
#include <dm/dm.hpp>
#include <datamunge/algorithms/gauss_seidel.hpp>
#include <datamunge/plot/diagram.hpp>
#include <array>
#include <cmath>
#include <filesystem>
#include <limits>
#include <print>
namespace dm=datamunge;
int main(){
 std::filesystem::create_directories("build");
 std::vector<double>dims,off,resprod;std::print("| n | assigned coordinates | off-diagonal products | residual products | norm evaluations | actual history entries |\n| ---: | ---: | ---: | ---: | ---: | ---: |\n");
 for(std::size_t n:std::array<std::size_t,7>{1,2,4,8,16,32,64}){const auto t=dm::algorithms::gauss_seidel_history(dm::algorithms::laplacian_1d_matrix(n),std::vector<double>(n,1),1,0,0);const auto&w=t.run.work;
  std::print("| {} | {} | {} | {} | {} | {} |\n",n,w.coordinate_updates,w.off_diagonal_products,w.residual_products,w.residual_evaluations,t.captured_entries);dims.push_back(n);off.push_back(w.off_diagonal_products);resprod.push_back(w.residual_products);}
 bool denied=false,early=false,bad=false,online=false;try{(void)dm::algorithms::gauss_seidel_history({{2,-1},{-1,2}},{1,1},1,0,15);}catch(const std::length_error&){denied=true;}
 auto t=dm::algorithms::gauss_seidel_history({{2,-1},{-1,2}},{1,1},1,0,16);const auto final=t.run.solution.x;t.coordinates[0].after[0]=999;const bool owned=t.coordinates[1].before[0]==.5&&t.run.solution.x==final;
 try{(void)dm::algorithms::gauss_seidel_history({{2}},{0},5,0,2);}catch(const std::length_error&){early=true;}
 try{(void)dm::algorithms::gauss_seidel_history({{0}},{0},0,0,1);}catch(const std::invalid_argument&){bad=true;}
 try{(void)dm::algorithms::gauss_seidel_trace({{2}},{4},5,0,1);}catch(const std::length_error&){online=true;}
 const auto oldzero=dm::algorithms::gauss_seidel_trace({{2}},{0},5,0,1);const auto empty=dm::algorithms::gauss_seidel_history({},{},std::numeric_limits<int>::max(),0,1);
 std::print("\nWhole entries required {}; actual {}; cap 15 rejected {}; cap 16 admitted true; independent owned copies {}.\n",dm::algorithms::gauss_seidel_history_entries(2,1),t.captured_entries,denied,owned);
 std::print("Zero-RHS whole budget requires {}; cap 2 rejected {}; old online cap 1 admits initial success {}; old online cap 1 rejects a needed sweep {}.\n",dm::algorithms::gauss_seidel_history_entries(1,5),early,oldzero.solution.converged,online);
 std::print("Validation before quota {}; empty history entries {}; empty initially converged {}; empty coordinates {}.\n",bad,empty.captured_entries,empty.run.solution.converged,empty.coordinates.size());
 auto work=dm::graphics::RPlot::create();work.lines(dims,off,"Off-diagonal",{37,99,235},2).lines(dims,resprod,"Residual",{220,38,38},2).legend({"Off-diagonal","Residual"},{{37,99,235},{220,38,38}})
  .title("One dense sweep plus residual").xlab("Number of unknowns n").ylab("Executed products, including zeros").y_limits(0,5000);
 auto quota=dm::graphics::RPlot::barplot({16.,double(t.captured_entries),15.},{"Required","Captured","Rejected cap"});quota.title("Whole one-sweep history").xlab("").ylab("Entries, not bytes").y_limits(0,21);
 dm::graphics::RLayout::create(1,2).add(work).add(quota).size(1100,500).title("Counted arithmetic and history admission measure different resources").fit_panels().save_svg("build/seidel_work.svg");
 if(!denied||!owned||!early||!bad||!online||empty.captured_entries!=1)throw std::runtime_error("work, quota and ownership");
}
